{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zz7bmlqwayt4qivxkzdvinpvqrcb6fbe2euszflfxrofonfyehma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Summary\n\n**The Rust translation is byte-for-byte correct.** No divergences were found in the library itself; no changes to `translation/src/lib.rs` were needed.\n\n### Phase A — artifacts (`translation/`)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | All 5 C exports (`printLine`, `printIntLine`, `bad`, `good`, `driver`) — **symbol diff empty in both directions**. `driver.c` is the only translation unit and it is fully translated; nothing stubbed. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | Grepping the whole C tree for rejections yields **exactly one**: `printLine`'s `if(line != NULL)`. No returns, asserts, error enums, or range checks exist. 1 real row (E1) + 14 generic FFI-boundary rows (G1–G14). |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | No `[features]`, no flags, no globals, no `switch`/`#ifdef` — the axes are entry point × input shape × stdio buffering mode. 24 rows. |\n\n### Phases B/C/D — 52 tests, all via `libloading` on both `.so`s\n- **B (24 rows)**: randomised (seed `0x5EED1234ABCDF00D`) sweeps of the *low-level* entry points, not just `driver()` — full ±`i32` range, digit/power boundaries, `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`, all 255 non-NUL bytes, 1 MiB payloads straddling the stdio buffer, and 300 mixed 1–40-call scripts across 4 buffering modes. Each row asserts C≡Rust **and** C≡independent reference model, so no row can pass vacuously.\n- **C (15 rows)**: `printLine(NULL)`, zero/oversized lengths, `%n`/`%s` payloads proven to be data not format, invalid UTF-8, wide values truncated through the `int` ABI slot, extra register args to `void(void)`, and a write-failing `stdout` (asserting the *same* `ferror` flag, not just \"both failed\"). Out-of-range-enum is explicitly discharged: the API has no enum/flag parameter, so the class degenerates to \"any `i32`\", swept exhaustively at the boundaries.\n- **D**: `nm -D` diff empty in every configuration, plus `readelf` bind/type/visibility parity and `ldd -r` clean. `verify_all.sh` runs the whole suite across all feature combos × debug/release: **ALL CONFIGURATIONS PASSED**, zero warnings.\n\n### One thing worth flagging\nThe initial run showed 11 \"divergences\" that were **entirely harness artifacts** — libtest's own progress output was leaking into my `dup2`-based fd-1 capture. I replaced it with a swap of glibc's `stdout` `FILE*`, which both `.so`s' `printf`/`puts` go through while Rust's `println!`/libtest write to fd 1 directly. `tests/phase_a_selfcheck.rs` now contains negative controls proving the capture is non-empty, uncontaminated, and *does* fail on a deliberate mismatch — otherwise \"all green\" would have been meaningless.\n\nTwo benign, non-behavioural differences are documented rather than \"fixed\": GCC rewrites the C `printf(\"%s\\n\", s)` into `puts(s)` (so the C `.so` imports `puts`, the Rust one doesn't), and `bad()`'s discarded `intOne + intTwo` — the original CWE-482 defect — is faithfully preserved."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3293,"cache_read_input_tokens":108157,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3293,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef1b08c7-50c6-4c7e-afda-148fc2328227","uuid":"83a9b1b8-7bf7-4ae9-a250-abaaaadb01c9","timestamp":"2026-08-28T12:31:33.005Z"}
